    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0225" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/516: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-29T10:00:00-04:00">September 29, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>185. My 182 of September 24, 6 p.m. The Minister of Finance is apparently not yet
                    ready to discuss the matter with me, the delay as <pb facs="0226" n="216"
                        xml:id="pg216"/> explained by the Under Secretary being due to the
                    Minister’s desire to have in hand data from various sources.</p>
                <p>However, yesterday afternoon I pressed the matter with the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs<anchor n="6" xml:id="d216-f1"/> who said that he was sympathetic to
                    my viewpoint and asked me to give him a brief memorandum which he said that he
                    would support before the Minister of Finance. He added that the question
                    possessed broad political aspects which financial authorities were inclined to
                    overlook and declared that the conclusion of an agreement of even very limited
                    range would yet constitute an opening and helpful wedge for further mutual
                    concessions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d216-f1" n="6" xml:id="d216-f1-content">
                <p>Carlos Saavedra Lamas.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
